WEBVTT

00:04.000 --> 00:05.420
Please, my love...

00:06.960 --> 00:08.880
...won't you die with me?

00:10.710 --> 00:14.000
That grin's good enough to go viral.

00:14.250 --> 00:15.210
Really?!

00:15.880 --> 00:18.540
Viral on what kind of site?!

00:18.920 --> 00:20.210
You think it'll get tons of likes?

00:20.210 --> 00:21.460
Oh yeah, totally.

00:21.460 --> 00:23.710
Oh, gosh, what if it did?!

00:21.460 --> 00:24.380
At least they seem to be having a lot of fun.

00:34.540 --> 00:36.000
Smell that fresh air.

00:36.880 --> 00:39.500
I'm so glad we decided to go camping!

00:42.710 --> 00:46.080
On a Sunday in mid-April,
with the cherry blossoms starting to fall,

00:47.830 --> 00:50.380
and me still recovering from the club incident,

00:51.040 --> 00:54.040
Eiko and Yayoi-chan invited me to go camping.

00:55.380 --> 00:56.920
Thanks, Kei-kun.

00:58.210 --> 01:01.750
This trip is partially for Yayoi-chan, too.

01:01.750 --> 01:02.540
It is?

01:03.170 --> 01:08.130
I think it's hard for her to ask me to take her places
'cause she's living with me.

01:09.330 --> 01:13.040
And I'm hesitant to go alone with her,
so it's easier when we've got a big, strong guy with us!

01:13.290 --> 01:14.250
Eiko...

01:14.540 --> 01:17.790
Okay, I'm gonna make sure they have a great time!

01:17.790 --> 01:22.710
Wait, Eiko. You're not worried
about a boy spending the night with us?

01:22.880 --> 01:26.670
Not at all! Our virgin Kei-kun's too chicken
to try anything weird with us!

01:27.380 --> 01:29.420
You're right. There's no debating that.

01:29.710 --> 01:31.670
STOP IT!

01:31.750 --> 01:34.540
We'll go get dinner started!

01:38.000 --> 01:39.790
That should do it.

01:39.790 --> 01:42.500
Yayoi-chan, let's go catch our dinner!

01:42.500 --> 01:43.330
Catch it?

01:43.460 --> 01:44.210
Yep!

01:44.380 --> 01:45.170
Fish it up,

01:45.210 --> 01:46.040
cook it up,

01:46.210 --> 01:46.920
eat it up!

01:47.080 --> 01:47.920
That's the plan!

01:48.750 --> 01:52.250
Yes. Let's fish up a whole bucketful
and impress the hell out of Eiko.

01:52.630 --> 01:54.420
That's the spirit, Yayoi-chan!

02:01.880 --> 02:03.210
Of course nothing's biting...

02:05.630 --> 02:06.540
Keitaro.

02:08.080 --> 02:10.380
Did you make a decision yet?

02:12.540 --> 02:14.580
Sorry. I'm still thinking it over.

02:15.000 --> 02:16.250
What's the hang-up?

02:18.330 --> 02:21.130
I've been trying to imagine what going out
and catching spirits would look like,

02:21.420 --> 02:22.170
but...

02:22.960 --> 02:24.920
One thing keeps freaking me out.

02:27.580 --> 02:33.880
What if I get cursed again, and you get hurt, too?
It scares me to death just thinking about it.

02:35.750 --> 02:39.420
Especially knowing you've
got your whole future ahead of you.

02:40.420 --> 02:45.000
I'm a grown-up. I should be stopping you
from doing anything that puts your life at stake.

02:49.040 --> 02:51.880
Keitaro, let's see who can catch more trout.

02:51.880 --> 02:57.460
If I win, then you don't get to worry
about my mission again!

02:59.210 --> 03:03.540
I get to choose how I spend or ruin my life.

03:05.290 --> 03:08.460
Sure. You're on, then!

03:10.170 --> 03:10.790
Okay.

03:11.420 --> 03:12.790
All right, let's do it!

03:12.960 --> 03:13.830
Go!

03:26.960 --> 03:29.130
<b>NEITHER CAUGHT ANYTHING</b>

03:33.630 --> 03:34.960
Hey, guys!

03:35.290 --> 03:36.790
Ta-dah!

03:52.790 --> 03:54.960
I put Yayoi-chan to bed.

03:55.580 --> 03:56.420
Thanks.

03:58.080 --> 04:01.580
We had so much fun today, huh?

04:01.960 --> 04:02.750
Yeah.

04:05.380 --> 04:06.210
Eiko...

04:07.460 --> 04:11.460
You'd get rid of the curse if you could, right?

04:12.540 --> 04:14.790
Where's this coming from?

04:15.000 --> 04:18.630
Yayoi-chan told me we could rid ourselves
of our curse, so...

04:21.250 --> 04:24.830
I don't mind it, since we're the same.
But if we weren't, then yeah.

04:24.830 --> 04:27.330
Huh? What do you mean?

04:31.750 --> 04:33.670
Wanna go for a walk?

04:39.580 --> 04:40.710
Cold!

04:40.880 --> 04:42.710
Well, yeah, it's nighttime.

04:43.130 --> 04:44.380
Hey, Kei-kun!

04:46.040 --> 04:49.790
Weird question: do you know the difference
between studying and researching?

04:51.290 --> 04:55.040
Studying is learning knowledge
that's already been discovered.

04:55.210 --> 04:58.000
Researching is discovering
that knowledge in the first place.

04:59.250 --> 05:01.420
That difference is important to me,

05:03.170 --> 05:05.380
because I want to research the supernatural.

05:05.580 --> 05:07.670
Huh?! Wait, but then-

05:07.920 --> 05:13.040
I've already written down everything about my hand
and the experiences we've had so far,

05:13.250 --> 05:16.670
and done some research to see
if there's a scientific explanation for everything.

05:17.500 --> 05:23.380
I think understanding our condition is going to help us
figure out how to rid us of the curse.

05:24.830 --> 05:31.130
I'm sure you've wondered why I'm going
to all these places despite what happened to us.

05:31.580 --> 05:33.960
That was kinda the reason.

05:34.130 --> 05:36.880
I mean, sure, I love the scary aspect of it all, too.

05:36.880 --> 05:37.960
Yeah, I figured!

05:38.420 --> 05:43.290
But you don't need to go there
to do your research. You could get hurt.

05:43.580 --> 05:44.540
I know.

05:44.790 --> 05:47.130
But it's not just the supernatural that interests me.

05:47.830 --> 05:52.000
There's something else...
Someone else I want to research.

05:53.670 --> 05:54.630
Kei-kun...

05:57.290 --> 06:02.170
...I want to discover more about you.

06:06.630 --> 06:10.960
Wait, just... me?

06:12.420 --> 06:18.880
I never wanted to go through the trouble
of getting rid of the curse. I could live with it.

06:19.920 --> 06:22.630
But if you couldn't...

06:24.500 --> 06:30.170
Eiko, if I said I wanted to visit more
haunted locations, would you tell me not to go?

06:31.290 --> 06:32.630
Why do you ask?

06:33.080 --> 06:34.580
Because I'd need to do it.

06:35.880 --> 06:41.670
...Then I'd risk any dangerous situation
to find a spirit strong enough to end our curse.

06:43.210 --> 06:44.830
And that's because...

06:46.210 --> 06:47.920
Because I care about you a lot.

06:56.080 --> 06:57.460
Promise me something.

06:57.710 --> 06:58.500
Huh?

06:59.670 --> 07:05.040
Stay with me. Don't go off on your own.
Stay close, so we can work together.

07:05.920 --> 07:08.630
Promise me that, and I'll say yes.

07:09.210 --> 07:10.080
Okay.

07:12.000 --> 07:15.380
I might have to dive deep into the supernatural...

07:16.040 --> 07:17.670
but if it gets rid of our curse...

07:18.710 --> 07:19.830
I'll do it!

07:21.830 --> 07:23.040
I promise.

07:28.630 --> 07:30.500
It's getting chilly. Let's get back.

07:31.040 --> 07:31.710
Yeah.

07:36.460 --> 07:37.500
Is that...

07:39.250 --> 07:41.290
No! Someone just...

07:43.040 --> 07:44.580
What? They're still...

07:46.880 --> 07:48.790
What's wrong, Eiko?

07:49.290 --> 07:51.080
Huh? Nothing!

07:51.330 --> 07:55.210
Actually, Kei-kun, do you sense anything
from that bridge?

07:57.540 --> 07:58.630
Nope.

07:59.460 --> 08:01.460
Huh? Am I just seeing things?

08:02.710 --> 08:04.880
I guess I'm kind of tired...

08:33.210 --> 08:35.000
Wh-what the...

08:39.960 --> 08:40.830
Eiko?

08:43.710 --> 08:44.580
Eiko!

08:46.790 --> 08:49.460
I have to go to the bridge.

08:49.460 --> 08:51.080
What're you doing, Eiko?

08:50.130 --> 08:51.080
The bridge.

08:51.080 --> 08:52.330
Keep it down.

08:54.170 --> 08:55.250
Yayoi-chan!

08:57.880 --> 08:59.290
I have to go.

08:59.790 --> 09:00.380
I have to go to the bridge...

09:00.380 --> 09:03.250
She's being controlled.

09:00.380 --> 09:06.170
I have to go to the bridge... I have to go to the bridge...

09:03.880 --> 09:05.420
She hasn't been possesed.

09:06.170 --> 09:08.500
I didn't sense anything up until just now!

09:08.500 --> 09:09.750
Hurry...

09:09.750 --> 09:11.580
The spirit is calling to her.

09:09.750 --> 09:17.130
I have to go to the bridge... I have to go to the bridge...

09:12.040 --> 09:16.460
And spirits that play with the mind
can't be transferred to a mindless doll.

09:17.130 --> 09:19.170
Did Eiko mention anything?

09:19.750 --> 09:22.210
Yeah, she did. Something about the bridge.

09:20.750 --> 09:22.210
Hurry...

09:23.040 --> 09:27.210
The bridge... The bridge...

09:23.040 --> 09:28.920
The first thing I can think of,
is a spirit that forces people to jump from bridges.

09:29.710 --> 09:34.040
I have to go to the bridge... I have to go to the bridge...

09:30.580 --> 09:32.290
W-we have to help her!

09:34.420 --> 09:36.580
We have to guide Eiko to the bridge.

09:36.580 --> 09:37.710
Are you crazy?!

09:38.170 --> 09:42.040
We have to devour or capture the spirit
that's controlling her.

09:38.170 --> 09:43.080
I have to go to the bridge... I have to go to the bridge...

09:43.080 --> 09:45.540
Or she'll be stuck like this forever.

09:46.580 --> 09:48.330
I have to go there.

09:52.500 --> 09:54.920
Keep her safe up there, Keitaro.

09:56.290 --> 09:59.330
I'll take care of finding the culprit!

10:02.500 --> 10:06.380
Yayoi-chan, I sense a weak presence
in the middle of the bridge.

10:07.380 --> 10:08.250
Got it.

10:09.830 --> 10:10.500
I see it!

10:13.040 --> 10:14.750
Let's try to capture it.

10:15.710 --> 10:20.330
Wait, so before we've caught spirits
that possess things. How do we do it in this case?

10:20.830 --> 10:24.040
It's easy, as long as I know where to find it.

10:24.540 --> 10:25.880
All I've gotta do...

10:27.460 --> 10:28.710
...is toy with it!

10:29.920 --> 10:35.130
When spirits are in danger,
they find a living thing to hide in and possess.

10:37.380 --> 10:42.330
Weaken them enough and they'll always
go straight for a spirit magnet like you.

10:43.420 --> 10:47.250
Then we catch them with a nail-protected doll,

10:48.000 --> 10:52.290
and immediately put it in a bag full of pure salt!

10:52.880 --> 10:55.960
D-did we get it?

10:58.000 --> 10:58.790
Eiko!

11:01.420 --> 11:02.710
Hey! It's still...

11:04.420 --> 11:06.580
Wait, it's totally quiet.

11:07.080 --> 11:08.670
So this wasn't the one doing that?

11:15.460 --> 11:16.080
Wait a sec!

11:21.540 --> 11:23.130
Eiko, no!

11:27.000 --> 11:28.630
It's not just one spirit.

11:31.670 --> 11:32.630
<i>It's spirits!</i>

11:33.460 --> 11:37.460
They're ignoring Eiko and going straight for Keitaro!

11:38.920 --> 11:44.080
So Eiko was just bait. They weren't after her...

11:46.290 --> 11:47.170
Keitaro!

12:00.500 --> 12:01.420
Keitaro!

12:04.170 --> 12:04.960
Eiko!

12:12.670 --> 12:14.540
W-we're okay...

12:15.790 --> 12:17.540
Glad we prepped for that.

12:17.920 --> 12:18.540
Now, then.

12:26.210 --> 12:27.830
Caught and collected.

12:32.040 --> 12:36.830
Your choice: go in, or get eaten.

12:37.380 --> 12:38.790
I'll count to three.

12:39.830 --> 12:42.290
One, two...

12:44.290 --> 12:45.380
Caught one.

12:45.920 --> 12:49.330
There were around ten, so that means eight left.

12:49.920 --> 12:52.540
Keitaro was right about that.

12:52.880 --> 12:54.420
I need to get down to them.

12:55.040 --> 12:59.330
Both of us are safe.
Thank God we were ready for this to happen!

13:00.080 --> 13:03.290
The spirit tempts people to jump off the bridge.

13:03.790 --> 13:06.330
So we're going to tie a lifeline just in case.

13:06.330 --> 13:11.630
Got it. Where'd you get this super strong rope, though?

13:12.080 --> 13:13.880
I found it at an abandoned shrine.

13:14.080 --> 13:16.210
I get the feeling you didn't just "find" it.

13:16.380 --> 13:18.170
It was binding a real nasty spirit.

13:18.170 --> 13:22.830
I hate to ask, but what happened to that real nasty spirit?

13:24.130 --> 13:25.130
That's it there.

13:26.420 --> 13:27.790
Back to what I was saying.

13:28.790 --> 13:34.500
I see spirits with my eyes,
so when it's dark, it's hard for me to spot them.

13:35.290 --> 13:37.080
Do you sense anything, Keitaro?

13:39.040 --> 13:41.040
I sense something, but it's faint.

13:42.000 --> 13:45.540
I dunno how to put it... There's a lot of them.

13:46.790 --> 13:50.210
They're working together?
Or just happen to be in the same place...

13:51.210 --> 13:53.500
Sorry, I can't really tell...

13:54.080 --> 13:58.080
Then we'll just have to prep
to fight a group of spirits, too.

13:58.500 --> 14:01.040
Your dolls aren't going to be enough?

14:01.210 --> 14:01.880
Nope.

14:01.880 --> 14:04.380
In a one-on-one fight, the one who's stronger wins.

14:04.960 --> 14:09.290
But even strong spirits have
a tough time handling multiple attackers.

14:09.580 --> 14:12.630
It's the same with fighting people.
It's risky to fight a whole group at once.

14:13.330 --> 14:17.630
I'm just one person, and we can estimate
there's around ten of them.

14:19.040 --> 14:21.960
Ten? Then we're in real trouble...

14:23.790 --> 14:27.540
I'm scared, but I have to keep Eiko safe!

14:28.170 --> 14:30.080
I just need to get back to Yayoi-chan...

14:34.420 --> 14:35.170
No way...

14:44.250 --> 14:44.960
Eiko?

14:45.670 --> 14:47.790
Where are you going?

14:48.540 --> 14:50.790
It's so much safer here.

15:10.670 --> 15:11.540
Can't breathe!

15:13.380 --> 15:14.250
Eiko!

15:21.750 --> 15:27.290
Oh shit, oh shit, oh shit, oh shit, oh shit, oh shit!

15:27.290 --> 15:28.630
I'm getting possessed!

15:41.630 --> 15:43.500
<b>GOLD FLAKE SAKE</b>

15:41.790 --> 15:43.330
Keitaro, take this.

15:43.750 --> 15:44.710
Sacred sake?

15:44.960 --> 15:49.130
If you're ever getting possesed,
put it in your mouth. It'll force out the spirit.

15:54.210 --> 15:58.540
And if you spit it out onto a doll, you can capture it, too.

16:03.880 --> 16:06.080
Got it! That makes two!

16:06.460 --> 16:10.130
We'll have to fight their numbers with our own.

16:11.000 --> 16:15.170
I can put rice in sacks and tie them to make new dolls.

16:15.630 --> 16:18.670
They'll be enough to capture spirits.

16:19.880 --> 16:23.580
We'll make a bunch of them,
then capture each spirit one by one.

16:24.210 --> 16:30.000
That will whittle down their numbers
while increasing our own and giving us the advantage.

16:35.540 --> 16:38.920
It's so easy to catch them when they're distracted.

16:39.500 --> 16:43.500
So focused on their prey,
they don't realize they're being hunted.

16:44.380 --> 16:45.290
Yayoi-chan!

16:45.920 --> 16:46.880
Sorry I kept you waiting.

16:48.380 --> 16:50.170
Yayoi-chan's okay, too.

16:50.170 --> 16:52.880
Now we just have to rescue Eiko!

16:54.000 --> 16:56.420
This makes four we've caught so far.

16:58.040 --> 17:01.460
There are three over there, so we outnumber them now.

17:01.960 --> 17:04.830
But it looks like they're gonna
come at us with a vengeance.

17:05.500 --> 17:06.330
Huh?!

17:08.830 --> 17:10.290
It's four on six!

17:10.670 --> 17:11.540
Don't worry.

17:19.500 --> 17:21.420
I took care of something earlier.

17:23.420 --> 17:27.460
One of my favorites ate one and recovered its strength.

17:27.460 --> 17:32.210
Now we're evenly matched, five on five,
and one of ours is super powerful.

17:32.880 --> 17:34.790
Keitaro, hand me the dolls.

17:43.040 --> 17:44.460
<b>SPIRITS POSSESSING ITEMS CONFORM TO THE ITEM AND ITS STATE</b>

17:44.960 --> 17:48.210
I have enough dolls for all of you here.

17:48.790 --> 17:55.250
If you want to end their suffering,
then talk amongst yourselves and decide who should go.

18:00.130 --> 18:02.500
Caught me a whole bunch of spirits.

18:05.080 --> 18:08.250
She caught ten spirits, just like that...

18:08.460 --> 18:10.130
Let's get straight to business, then.

18:10.790 --> 18:14.040
Which one of you is controlling Eiko?

18:22.420 --> 18:24.040
I don't like liars.

18:25.130 --> 18:30.000
If you don't want the wrong person to die,
then I suggest you tell the truth.

18:40.790 --> 18:45.630
She's making them fight amongst themselves,
showing them what happens to traitors...

18:45.630 --> 18:47.580
Showing them she's the boss.

18:47.790 --> 18:48.670
I'll kill you.

18:49.630 --> 18:53.080
I'll kill you! I'll kill you! I'll kill you!

18:53.080 --> 18:55.250
I'll send you straight to Hell!

18:55.580 --> 19:00.130
I've already seen Hell. Want me to show you?

18:57.500 --> 19:00.130
I'll kill you! I'll kill you!

19:00.330 --> 19:02.630
Go stack stones in the underworld, you little brat!

19:02.920 --> 19:04.670
No, I insist.

19:05.830 --> 19:07.500
I'll make it simple for you.

19:08.000 --> 19:11.540
It's going to be where you live
for the rest of your pitiful existence!

19:20.960 --> 19:21.960
Eiko!

19:24.210 --> 19:25.750
That should've stopped it.

19:29.670 --> 19:32.750
Wait, all that happened?!

19:33.210 --> 19:35.670
Gosh, I don't remember anything.

19:35.960 --> 19:40.000
That's probably for the best.
Sometimes, amnesia is a blessing.

19:40.790 --> 19:46.330
You just rest till morning.
Yayoi-chan and I will handle the rest.

19:46.750 --> 19:50.290
Wait, what?! Are you serious?!

20:04.880 --> 20:07.000
Kei-kun! Morning!

20:07.000 --> 20:09.250
Morning. How're you feeling?

20:09.500 --> 20:11.500
Great, super-duper!

20:11.500 --> 20:14.460
Good. That's a relief.

20:25.460 --> 20:26.080
Eiko?

20:27.710 --> 20:30.330
I still don't remember what happened last night.

20:30.830 --> 20:32.790
But I did catch onto something.

20:33.540 --> 20:35.460
This familiar warmth.

20:37.880 --> 20:41.330
I'm guessing you had to go through hell last night.

20:41.920 --> 20:45.330
But the whole time, you made sure I was safe.

20:45.330 --> 20:51.710
N-nah, I messed up and got you dragged into everything!
I should be thanking you.

20:51.710 --> 20:53.040
Don't be humble.

20:55.580 --> 20:56.420
Okay.

20:58.290 --> 21:01.580
I was scared, but I made a promise.

21:02.630 --> 21:05.540
So I pushed through.

21:08.130 --> 21:09.130
Thank you.

21:13.540 --> 21:14.710
I love you, you know.

21:20.130 --> 21:21.250
Me, too.

21:22.080 --> 21:24.330
I love you, too.

21:26.830 --> 21:31.250
So I promise, no matter what happens,
or what we get tangled up in,

21:32.170 --> 21:34.290
I will always come to save you.

21:35.920 --> 21:36.830
Good.

21:37.750 --> 21:40.500
Kei-kun, I've got you now.

21:45.630 --> 21:47.500
Yayoi-chan, I've made my decision.

21:48.000 --> 21:49.790
I'll help you catch spirits.

21:50.790 --> 21:51.670
You sure?

21:52.330 --> 21:53.080
I'm sure.

21:53.080 --> 21:57.880
I thought diving into the supernatural
would keep me from living a normal life,

21:58.790 --> 22:01.170
but I was totally wrong about
how those two things were related.

22:01.830 --> 22:06.630
I'm going to make friends AND learn how to deal with
my supernatural magnetism.

22:07.040 --> 22:12.040
Then I'll get rid of the curse
and start a new life with a clean slate.

22:13.250 --> 22:14.540
It's that simple.

22:15.630 --> 22:18.830
All this time, I was so afraid
of getting other people tangled up in this,

22:19.040 --> 22:21.210
so I thought it was better to be alone.

22:22.750 --> 22:23.460
But now,

22:24.500 --> 22:27.210
I can push through that fear
because I want to protect the ones I love!

22:31.830 --> 22:33.960
Y'know, it's taken so long.

22:35.000 --> 22:37.460
Recommending the tutoring place,

22:38.080 --> 22:42.710
then pushing for Kei-kun to be Yayoi-chan's tutor
to bring them together.

22:43.920 --> 22:48.710
This curse has finally tied the two of us together.

22:50.460 --> 22:54.790
Let's go follow our fear, together,
like we did before what happened to us!

22:56.080 --> 22:59.960
We'll exit the living world,
cross the River Styx hand in hand,

23:00.290 --> 23:10.130
and slit open the belly of the supernatural
to discover its secrets and make them known!

23:14.170 --> 23:18.170
Kei-kun, I've got you now!

23:21.630 --> 23:33.710
Yayoi and Keitaro team up to gather spirits,
one to save her mother, the other to remove a curse.

23:35.040 --> 23:39.330
Next, they head for a haunted site within the city
that is sure to terrify...
